   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear STAN team and users,</div><div><br></div><div>I tried re-implemented some of the GARMA models, see</div><div>Malaria GARMA models link at the end of the email. </div><div>However without success. </div><div><br></div><div>I simplified the model and ended with an very basic</div><div>Poisson AR(1) model, with is close to the 2nd model in the </div><div>2nd link.</div><div><br></div><div>The pairs plot looks not so good, but I have no idea how</div><div>to fix the correlations between the parameters. </div><div><br></div><div>I spent nearly a full day of altering the model in various ways.</div><div>I even implemented the ZQ2 model, where the count data</div><div>is replaced by log(y+c), for the 0 case. Some things, that might</div><div>not harmonize good together, might be the normal and the</div><div>poisson distributions. </div><div><br></div><div>Any help or hint would be very helpful. </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks a lot in advance,</div><div>Andre</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m using RSTAN2.7.0 on Ubuntu 14.04, standard installation.</div><div><br><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><span style=\"font-size:13.8666667938232px;line-height:16.6399993896484px\"><span style=\"color:#000\">mu </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.21</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>sigma </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.15</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>phi </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>T </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:10.4pt!important;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></span></font><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></span><span style=\"color:blue;font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;line-height:1.2;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:#008\">print</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pars</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;mu&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;phi&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;sigma&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Inference</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Stan</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> GAR</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chains</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> each </span><span style=\"color:#008\">with</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> iter</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> warmup</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">500</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> thin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>post</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">warmup draws per chain</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">500</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> total post</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">warmup draws</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2000.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>      mean se_mean   sd </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">25</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">75</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">97.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n_eff </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Rhat</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>mu    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.42</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.00</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.04</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.35</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.40</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.42</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.45</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.50</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">182</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.02</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>phi   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.05</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.00</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.02</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.02</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.04</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.05</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.06</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.08</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">316</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.02</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>sigma </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.26</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.01</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.04</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.16</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.23</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.26</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.29</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.34</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">26</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.17</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Samples</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> were drawn </span><span style=\"color:#008\">using</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NUTS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">diag_e</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> at </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sun</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Aug</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">23</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">04</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">06</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2015.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">For</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> each parameter</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> n_eff </span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> a crude measure of effective sample size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">and</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Rhat</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> the potential scale reduction factor on split chains </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">at <br>convergence</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Rhat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">).</span></pre></span></div></code></div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-xnnCMIOMAu8/VdoPmXup2rI/AAAAAAAAAnY/GzrTvKaZAJ0/s1600/Rplot.png\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-xnnCMIOMAu8/VdoPmXup2rI/AAAAAAAAAnY/GzrTvKaZAJ0/s1600/Rplot.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463873558000&amp;usg=AOvVaw38RhID8OkpWVE2vu9UcXfi\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-xnnCMIOMAu8/VdoPmXup2rI/AAAAAAAAAnY/GzrTvKaZAJ0/s320/Rplot.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\"></a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Links: </div><div>Proof of Expected Value and Variance of AR(1) <br></div><div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autoregressive_model\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autoregressive_model&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463873558000&amp;usg=AOvVaw234bDFVlaKE0Ye8ez4p_dC\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autoregressive_model</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Initial point variance (see Model 2)</div><div><a href=\"http://www.dme.ufrj.br/mcmc/AR1model-WinBUGS.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.dme.ufrj.br/mcmc/AR1model-WinBUGS.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463873558000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1eDADTccl3UeosQa_TUWyo\">http://www.dme.ufrj.br/mcmc/AR1model-WinBUGS.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Malaria GARMA Models</div><div><a href=\"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3681978/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3681978/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463873558000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2FWK-AFVTAWY_3It5Dz7-k\">http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3681978/</a></div></div>"
    ]
