    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear STAN team and users,</div><div><br></div><div>I tried re-implemented some of the GARMA models, see</div><div>Malaria GARMA models link at the end of the email. </div><div>However without success. </div><div><br></div><div>I simplified the model and ended with an very basic</div><div>Poisson AR(1) model, with is close to the 2nd model in the </div><div>2nd link.</div><div><br></div><div>The pairs plot looks not so good, but I have no idea how</div><div>to fix the correlations between the parameters. </div><div><br></div><div>I spent nearly a full day of altering the model in various ways.</div><div>I even implemented the ZQ2 model, where the count data</div><div>is replaced by log(y+c), for the 0 case. Some things, that might</div><div>not harmonize good together, might be the normal and the</div><div>poisson distributions. </div><div><br></div><div>Any help or hint would be very helpful. </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks a lot in advance,</div><div>Andre</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m using RSTAN2.7.0 on Ubuntu 14.04, standard installation.</div><div><br><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;border-width:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span><font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><span style=\"font-size:13.8666667938232px;line-height:16.6399993896484px\"><span>mu </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.21</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span><br>sigma </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.15</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span><br>phi </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span><br>T </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:10.4pt!important;line-height:1.2\"><span><br><br></span></span></font><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span> </span></span><span style=\"color:blue;font-family:&#39;Ubuntu Mono&#39;;font-size:10.4pt!important;line-height:1.2;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"color:#008\">print</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span>pars</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;mu&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;phi&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;sigma&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span><br></span></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Inference</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Stan</span><span> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span> GAR</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span><br></span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span> chains</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> each </span><span style=\"color:#008\">with</span><span> iter</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span> warmup</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">500</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span> thin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span> <br>post</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span>warmup draws per chain</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">500</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> total post</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span>warmup draws</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2000.</span><span><br><br>      mean se_mean   sd </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span>  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">25</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span>  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span>  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">75</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">97.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span> n_eff </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Rhat</span><span><br>mu    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.42</span><span>    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.00</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.04</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.35</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.40</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.42</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.45</span><span>  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.50</span><span>   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">182</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.02</span><span><br>phi   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.05</span><span>    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.00</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.02</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.02</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.04</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.05</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.06</span><span>  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.08</span><span>   </span><span style=\"color:#066\">316</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.02</span><span><br>sigma </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.26</span><span>    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.01</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.04</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.16</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.23</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.26</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.29</span><span>  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.34</span><span>    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">26</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.17</span><span><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Samples</span><span> were drawn </span><span style=\"color:#008\">using</span><span> NUTS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>diag_e</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span> at </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sun</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Aug</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">23</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">04</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">06</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2015.</span><span><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">For</span><span> each parameter</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> n_eff </span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span> a crude measure of effective sample size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">and</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Rhat</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span> the potential scale reduction factor on split chains </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>at <br>convergence</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Rhat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">).</span></pre></span></div></code></div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-xnnCMIOMAu8/VdoPmXup2rI/AAAAAAAAAnY/GzrTvKaZAJ0/s1600/Rplot.png\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-xnnCMIOMAu8/VdoPmXup2rI/AAAAAAAAAnY/GzrTvKaZAJ0/s1600/Rplot.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463873570000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2UMrzoO_a3B142WztHFejM\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-xnnCMIOMAu8/VdoPmXup2rI/AAAAAAAAAnY/GzrTvKaZAJ0/s320/Rplot.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"180\"></a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Links: </div><div>Proof of Expected Value and Variance of AR(1) <br></div><div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autoregressive_model\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autoregressive_model&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463873570000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1TXzYDWlYbzefniW38LuCh\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autoregressive_model</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Initial point variance (see Model 2)</div><div><a href=\"http://www.dme.ufrj.br/mcmc/AR1model-WinBUGS.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.dme.ufrj.br/mcmc/AR1model-WinBUGS.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463873570000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2tmJvPSc8GvPQOY_ck4sDM\">http://www.dme.ufrj.br/mcmc/AR1model-WinBUGS.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Malaria GARMA Models</div><div><a href=\"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3681978/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3681978/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463873570000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0x_iFXiSLVaKDlct5UgBNM\">http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3681978/</a></div></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
