    [
     3,
     "\r<br>&gt; On Aug 24, 2015, at 5:29 AM, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">andre.p...@googlemail.com</a> wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Dear Ben, Andrew, STAN users,\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; the model works perfectly fine now. I attached the to whoever wants to use it.\r<br>&gt; Feel free, for any purpose.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; The ARMA model on: \r<br>&gt; 6.4 pg. 84 2.7.0 shows: \r<br>&gt; nu[1] &lt;- mu + phi * mu;   // assume err[0] == 0\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Isn&#39;t with err[0] == 0 the model AR(1) and thus nu[1] should be \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; nu[1] &lt;- mu / (1-phi); \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Here&#39;s a link to Expected Value of ARMA(1,1):\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"http://mathhelpforum.com/advanced-statistics/178529-expected-value-variance-arma-1-1-model.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mathhelpforum.com/advanced-statistics/178529-expected-value-variance-arma-1-1-model.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463873574000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3NME3YlV0ZB22ZYt1e2p-Y\">http://mathhelpforum.com/advanced-statistics/178529-expected-value-variance-arma-1-1-model.html</a>\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt;  I changed Ben&#39;s suggestions slightly: \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt;   for (t in 2:T)  nu[t] &lt;- mu + phi * nu[t-1] + sigma * nu_z[t];\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Andre \r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
